 Not the usual git add . && git commit stuff. These are real-world puzzles every DevOps / Developer faces 👇

🔹 𝟭. 𝗕𝗿𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗵𝗶𝗻𝗴 & 𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸𝗳𝗹𝗼𝘄
 1️⃣ You started coding directly on main instead of a feature branch — how do you fix it without losing work?
 2️⃣ You’re asked to create a release branch with only selected commits from develop. How would you do that?

🔹 𝟮. 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝗳𝗹𝗶𝗰𝘁 𝗛𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗴
 1️⃣ You hit the same merge conflict every time you merge two branches. How can you stop this loop?
 2️⃣ You’re in the middle of a messy rebase — how do you abort safely and roll back?

🔹 𝟯. 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗺𝗶𝘁 𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗴𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁
 1️⃣ You want to split one commit into two smaller ones. Which commands will you use?
 2️⃣ You pushed a commit with the wrong message to a shared branch. How do you fix it without breaking history?

🔹 𝟰. 𝗖𝗼𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗯𝗼𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 & 𝗧𝗲𝗮𝗺 𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸𝗳𝗹𝗼𝘄𝘀
 1️⃣ A teammate’s commit broke develop. How do you quickly revert only that commit?
 2️⃣ You need to test a teammate’s branch locally without merging it. What’s the best approach?

